## What changed

- added `docs/llama-cpp-runtime-optimization-plan.md` as the canonical target for upstream qualification, CPU efficiency, recurrent/prefix-state qualification, backend/device capability reporting, OpenCL/Adreno, KV-cache experiments, evaluation-only batching, deterministic execution planning and deferred Hexagon/HTP work;
- added explicit P0/P1/P2/P3 priority ordering relative to the active OMBRA, Qwen3.5, memory, shared-runtime, reference-architecture and model-evaluation plans;
- kept Harness 0.5 CPU-first and the current llama.cpp pin frozen by default unless a correctness/security blocker justifies a controlled update;
- made Qwen3.5 recurrent/prefix/session reuse a correctness qualification rather than silently enabling it from generic llama.cpp API availability;
- aligned stale repository-roadmap summary entries with the current Qwen3.5, memory-management, shared-runtime, OMBRA and reference-architecture ledgers;
- indexed the new canonical source in `docs/README.md`.

## Why

The current repository already exposes many llama.cpp knobs, but the highest-value follow-on work spans multiple existing owners. This change gives that work one bounded plan while preserving repo-template-sw invariants: one owner per fact, evidence before hardware/performance claims, no duplicate runtime policy and no speculative expansion that destabilizes the current release lane.

## Priority effect

P0 remains the existing release/evidence lane: OMB-6B/OMB-8, Q35-6/Q35-7, MEM-7/MEM-8, SR-6 and Harness 0.5. The new llama.cpp work begins at P1 with qualification and semantics-preserving CPU improvements. Adreno OpenCL and related hardware experiments are P2; Hexagon/HTP is P3/deferred.

## Validation

- inspected the remote diff against current `dev` and confirmed the branch is based directly on the current integration line;
- new target-specification is 202 lines, below the repository `target-specification` line budget;
- required active-document metadata and documentation-map reachability are present;
- no runtime/code behavior is changed by this PR.

